"r4rk1/1b1nbppp/1qp1pn2/p7/PpBPP3/5N2/1P1BQPPP/R1NR2K1 b - -":{"variation":"pure-slav","moves":[{"uci":"c6c5","book":true,"notes":[{"text":"This is the usual Pure Slav position: you counter the center and press on the b6-f2 diagonal.","original":"This is most usual position to get from \"Pure Slav\".\nBlack proceeds with countering the center and pressing on b6-f2 diagonal.\nRooks will come to d and f file.\nWhite will try to push center pawns ahead and keep the blacks LSB closed.\nRooks will also come on d and c file and knight on b3."}]}]},
"rnbqkb1r/pp2pppp/2p2n2/8/P1pP4/2N2N2/1P2PPPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq -":{"variation":"pure-slav","moves":[{"uci":"c8f5","book":true,"notes":[{"text":"With a4, White gave up the e4 square for a while; your bishop develops naturally and you stand well.","original":"5. a4 has a problem and that problem is that white gives up his e4 square for some time. Black naturally develops his LSB on a natural square and has a good game.","ideas":[{"type":"purpose","from":"f5","relation":"controls","targets":["e4"]}]}]}]},
